{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46837-non-scion-supernaturals-fatebonding-and-mortal-beliefs","id":46837,"title":"Non-Scion supernaturals, Fatebonding, and Mortal beliefs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-11T05:12:57-08:00","id":46837,"title":"Non-Scion supernaturals, Fatebonding, and Mortal beliefs","content":"How exactly does it work, when non-Scion supernaturals assume a Fatebonded persona that has mortal belief attached to it?<br /> <br /> For instance, a brony Scion of Artemis (born from a lesbian tryst the goddess had with his mother) is given the ability to summon the goddess's Pegasus mare as a Birthright. He then proceeds to dye her mane and tail pink, (re-)name her Fluttershy, cast a 1-dot Magic Spell on her (to create a Fatebond between them), and then feed her a measure of his blood to give her human-like intelligence. What would happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T06:30:36-08:00","id":46855,"title":"","content":"If you sat down with your storyteller and mutually agreed that this would be a brony-centric or slapstick campaign then chances are good that the Pegasus might begin to embrace the role of Fluttershy that you are trying to associate her with. After all, as a PC it is your job to eventually do the impossible through hardship and slow accumulation of plot tokens until your eventual triumph (and since you are Greek, your eventual tragedy as well).<br /> <br /> If you sprung this on your storyteller without forewarning, and it is not a brony-centric or slapstick campaign, then chances are good that Artemis or one of her lower legend representatives would like to have a word with you about Greek aesthetics of beauty and defacing what is quite literally a living piece of art (Pegasus). Additionally Pegasus, already being a creature of some intelligence, may or may not take exception to the added colors depending on its mood and your social attributes. More importantly nothing much would happen because by RAW legendary creatures do not take on fated roles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 01-11-2014, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T06:32:37-08:00","id":46857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46837-non-scion-supernaturals-fatebonding-and-mortal-beliefs?p=46855#post46855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you sat down with your storyteller and mutually agreed that this would be a brony-centric or slapstick campaign then chances are good that the Pegasus might begin to embrace the role of Fluttershy that you are trying to associate her with. After all, as a PC it is your job to eventually do the impossible through hardship and slow accumulation of plot tokens until your eventual triumph (and since you are Greek, your eventual tragedy as well).<br /> <br /> If you sprung this on your storyteller without forewarning, and it is not a brony-centric or slapstick campaign, then chances are good that Artemis or one of her lower legend representatives would like to have a word with you about Greek aesthetics of beauty and defacing what is quite literally a living piece of art (Pegasus). Additionally Pegasus, already being a creature of some intelligence, may or may not take exception to the added colors depending on its mood and your social attributes. More importantly nothing much would happen because by RAW, because legendary creatures do not take on fated roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention there's no real RAW ability to give a creature human-like intelligence; especially not with one's own blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T06:50:31-08:00","id":46870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46837-non-scion-supernaturals-fatebonding-and-mortal-beliefs?p=46855#post46855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you sprung this on your storyteller without forewarning, and it is not a brony-centric or slapstick campaign, then chances are good that Artemis or one of her lower legend representatives would like to have a word with you about Greek aesthetics of beauty and defacing what is quite literally a living piece of art (Pegasus). Additionally Pegasus, already being a creature of some intelligence, may or may not take exception to the added colors depending on its mood and your social attributes. More importantly nothing much would happen because by RAW legendary creatures do not take on fated roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the original Pegasus, one of his dozen offspring that don't even have Legend scores, and are just winged horses with Greek Virtues. The ones on p. 326-327 of Scion: Hero. I'd be more worried about Artemis being pissed off about her noble steed suddenly gaining a great distaste for seeing animals being injured, personally, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46837-non-scion-supernaturals-fatebonding-and-mortal-beliefs?p=46857#post46857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention there's no real RAW ability to give a creature human-like intelligence; especially not with one's own blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 143 of Scion: Companion. Technically, any body fluid that contains ichor will do, but unless you want to try fucking a horse...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1878,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","user":"AdamantineRapier","date":". 01-11-2014, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T07:00:40-08:00","id":46876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamantineRapier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46837-non-scion-supernaturals-fatebonding-and-mortal-beliefs#post46837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly does it work, when non-Scion supernaturals assume a Fatebonded persona that has mortal belief attached to it?<br /> <br /> For instance, a brony Scion of Artemis (born from a lesbian tryst the goddess had with his mother) is given the ability to summon the goddess's Pegasus mare as a Birthright. He then proceeds to dye her mane and tail pink, (re-)name her Fluttershy, cast a 1-dot Magic Spell on her (to create a Fatebond between them), and then feed her a measure of his blood to give her human-like intelligence. What would happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Non-Scion Supernaturals (and if I remember correctly, Scions) do not assume Fated roles by default. So, nothing would happen.<br /> <br /> And while I wholeheartedly support the idea of your character following his dreams, please remember that the Greek Gods have very, <i>very</i>, narrow ideas of what does and does not look good. Artemis might very well take offence at your efforts, so be sure to clear it with her (and, definitely, the Pegasus itself) first. And let us not forget what happened to the last mortal man who offended Artemis (Actaeon).<br /> <br /> Also, where did you get the idea of feeding the animal your blood to make it intelligent? I keep thinking Jotunblut, but A. He's Greek, so he shouldn't have it and B. Jotunblut can't affect mental stats iirc.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Sorry, didn't see you'd already replied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 01-11-2014, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T07:05:27-08:00","id":46879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamantineRapier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46837-non-scion-supernaturals-fatebonding-and-mortal-beliefs?p=46870#post46870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the original Pegasus, one of his dozen offspring that don't even have Legend scores, and are just winged horses with Greek Virtues. The ones on p. 326-327 of Scion: Hero. I'd be more worried about Artemis being pissed off about her noble steed suddenly gaining a great distaste for seeing animals being injured, personally, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Those winged horses have Legend ratings of 3 each. They are Legendary creatures, and thus, cannot assume a persona.<br /> <br /> Which, incidentally, also disqualifies them from becoming Companions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 01-11-2014, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T07:08:27-08:00","id":46882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamantineRapier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46837-non-scion-supernaturals-fatebonding-and-mortal-beliefs?p=46870#post46870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the original Pegasus, one of his dozen offspring that don't even have Legend scores, and are just winged horses with Greek Virtues. The ones on p. 326-327 of Scion: Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean one of the 12 immortal offspring? The companion rules on page 143 are only for mortals.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamantineRapier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46837-non-scion-supernaturals-fatebonding-and-mortal-beliefs?p=46870#post46870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 143 of Scion: Companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, she specified 'creature' which rarely involves anything mortal. I mean, it is technically possible to take a mortal as part of your creature birthright... it is just extremely uncommon from my anecdotal experience. The few times I have seen it, the mortal creature ends up becoming more than mortal very quickly.<br /> <br /> Not that the Companion rules should be taken seriously of course.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T07:29:53-08:00","id":46891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamantineRapier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46837-non-scion-supernaturals-fatebonding-and-mortal-beliefs#post46837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly does it work, when non-Scion supernaturals assume a Fatebonded persona that has mortal belief attached to it?<br /> <br /> For instance, a brony Scion of Artemis (born from a lesbian tryst the goddess had with his mother) is given the ability to summon the goddess's Pegasus mare as a Birthright. He then proceeds to dye her mane and tail pink, (re-)name her Fluttershy, cast a 1-dot Magic Spell on her (to create a Fatebond between them), and then feed her a measure of his blood to give her human-like intelligence. What would happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>The player gets smacked upside the head. Repeatedly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}